Z||000009||Master_Sushi||11-02-2001||09:37 PM||||You’d think self checkouts would cause allot of theft. I saw one of these at k-mart a few days ago. I would think like ½ the people don’t scan in things and bag them. Do they have a camera watching or something??<P>How do they work to anyone that used them? Do they take cash?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||11-02-2001||10:33 PM||||They installed about 3-4 of those machines at my super kmart.  Yes there are different kmarts in illinois.<P>it was about 6 months ago when they did this new thing.  Superkmarts are 24hour grocery/kmart stores.<P>the machines are used for express lines.  Im not sure about the current status.<P><BR>Im a cashier at a grocery store, and when i went to one of the machines.  i had to figure out how to use it.  The touch screens are not too sensitive.  And the process is a lot slower then a real cashier.  <P>They have to be monitoring to prevent merchandise from being stolen.  I know they have cameras above, but i dont know if its 24-7.  Theres no way of stealing money, the money is inserted in the machine and change is given out.   I would think that "fake" scanning and putting in the bag would work.  Unless they are keeping track of what your doing.<P>I can get 3-4 customers out of my line, for the time it takes to get one from an auto system.  This is for short orders.  And i will still be faster on big orders.  <P>The customers are not aware of operating the machine.  They have to scan their own items.  Scanning isn't easy if you havn't done it before.  This slows the process down, compared to someone that knows how to scan and where the barcodes are located.  Customers have to bag the items after they scan it, which takes more time.  Plus, putting money in the machine is a lot slower then handing a cashier the bills+change.  Unless a credit/debit card is used.<P><BR>Its a good idea, only if one or two machines are used, for express lines.  But i wouldn't want to wait 30minutes for people in front of me to check out in $100 or more orders.||||reg||1
Z||000011||frontal lobe||11-02-2001||10:41 PM||||K-mart is one of the few places where having do-it-yourself checkout is actually an UPGRADE in service, when you compare it to who you usually had checking you out.<P>I think Tom Cruise said it best in the movie Rainman.||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroFanaticus2||11-02-2001||11:17 PM||||Hmmm...<BR>So, what would happen if you were to 'accidentally' put something in the cart that didn't 'exactly' scan?<P>I haven't seen these things yet so I don't know what or how exactly they work.  But seems to me that it's a worthless idea that'll get thrown out in a year or two.  What ever happened to customer service?  Even if it is an underage dimwit that can't pronounce his words correctly, atleast they know how to use the loud speaker to get someone who can help.... Plus, it's healthy to vent at an actual person instead of an emotionless machine.<P>BTW, I've actually had some really good customer service from some of the K-Mart employees in my area.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||11-03-2001||01:10 AM||||instead of using these stupid do it yourself scanners, why dont they build Kmart stores like a giant candy vending machine.<P> I could be about 5 stories high and 50 feet wide, all behind a giant window.<P> you look throught the glass and see what you want - there it is, a ten pack of hanes T shirts, mens large, $5.99<P> so you put a $10 bill in the currency reader, and it spits it back out, and you do this about 8 more times and finally it accepts it<P> then you push DFZR89354 for the item you want - and the big metal screw thing turns and your package of underwear falls 3 stories into the giant slot. and your change in quarters falls down.<P> sounds like a better system to me.||||reg||11
Z||000014||frontal lobe||11-03-2001||02:21 AM||||Awesome idea, but then you put your money in and turn the knob, and the underwear get hung up and don't drop and you are out of luck.  You have to go to customer service (service, ha).  Oh boy, here we go.  Have to deal with people again.<P>Here in Wisconsin, K-mart has about the worst service of any chain.  Target is MUCH better.  Even wally-mart.||||reg||1
