Z||000016||Nashco||11-03-2001||04:03 AM||||Hey!  I actually like the automatic do-it-yourself scanners.  You see, in Flint....basically anything that involves customer service and the general public together sucks!<P>The ones they installed at the Kessel in Flint is actually quite high tech.  It has the weight of every item saved in a database.  When you scan the item, you put it in the bag, while the system tracks the weight change of the bag.  If you don't scan something, it alerts the cashier that there's a problem.  If you scan two things, and don't put them down into the bag, it will alert the cashier.  I've never had to wait on the system after I figured it out the first time.<P>The do-it-yourself line is usually non-existent...bonus.  It has very clear, easily operated push screen functions, the ability to take cash, credit, debit, coupons, etc.  I can also operate the machine about 10 times faster than the average clerk scans the items there (they're paid hourly, why should they care?...the attitude there is gross).  So, overall, I can cut my checkout time from about ten minutes to about 3 minutes....why not?<P>I pray Walmart gets these down here in 'bama very soon.  I don't know how well the general populus would pick up on the high-tech gadgetry, but I don't care either.  If I can use it, great.  The lines are ridiculous, sometimes taking 20 minutes during normal traffic.  I don't even go there when it's busy, I couldn't imagine being there during THAT.  Walmart cashiers down here also like the hourly pay rate, I can tell.  They must not have any bonuses for scanning items faster or anything.<P>I worked at a grocery store before, and they had bonuses for the quicker employees.  The employees really were affected by this, as it came fun and semi-competitive to see who could scan quickly and maintain composure with the customer.<P>Ok..enough of that..I'm all for these checkout systems.  They're efficient if they're modern, and the user has half a brain.  If their system sucks, they pay the price by losing customers, as they should.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroKyle||11-03-2001||04:42 PM||||Meijer has them for the express lane. I find them much faster than dealing with the old lady that carefully but surely scans everything, then waits for a bagger to bag it. Gets me in and out quicker and it doesn't ever count my money wrong.||||reg||1
